the top story this afternoon more  injuries for the star-crossed san  francisco 49ers  look last year it was not easy for them  to get near the top of the mountain they  had to fight and scratch and claw all  the way to week 17. yes they had a  special season there were no gimmies  along the way there were a few blowouts  they had to deal with the seahawks they  had to deal with the rams they had to  deal with the cardinals they had to deal  with teams like the vikings and packers  in the playoffs and ultimately couldn't  overcome the chiefs this year they can't  overcome the injuries george kittle star  tight end out eight weeks with a broken  bone in his foot that happened yesterday  in the loss to the seattle seahawks and  jimmy garoppolo  high ankle sprain again  out at least a month this time  the 49ers  and this is stunning  and maybe this will help the 49ers in  deciding what to do at the quarterback  position after this year  they're 24 and 9  in games that jimmy garoppolo starts  and five and 21 when someone else starts  since uh the 2017 season that's stunning  to me  it's very stunning mike and  it feels like like i was looking up nick  mullen's record while ago it feels like  he's better than what he is he's four  and six he went one and one this year  but it just seems like he's played  better than that but obviously he hasn't  and the 49ers can't seem to win without  jimmy g and you know whatever they do  with the quarterback position whether  it's jimmy or somebody else after this  season it certainly doesn't need to be  one of these backups they're not the  same team when it's nick mullins or cj  beathard in the lineup but you know you  do wonder mike if the 49ers put jimmy  garoppolo back in the lineup too soon  after the heinkel sprain the first time  he played through it in the jets game  missed a couple games came back in that  week five game it was obvious against  the dolphins he shouldn't have been  playing and then the next week he looked  right again so they probably put him out  there too quick did that lead to lip to  this it does make you wonder whether  they should have kept him out longer let  that thing fully heal and now here we  are again maybe it wouldn't have made a  difference who knows but you do wonder  that with what he's going through now  but this is just it seemed like almost a  daily occurrence for the 49ers one  injury after another injury and i don't  know how you get through all these  injuries and and make the playoffs and  and they've talked about  getting back as nfc champions they  talked about that since the point in the  super bowl last year and now here we are  they're gonna have a tough time doing  that with all these injuries  i think the analysis when it comes to  garoppolo and his injury was fairly  simple they balanced an impaired  garoppolo against a healthy  nick mullins or a healthy cj beathard  and they decided to roll the dice with  an injured jimmy garoppolo it didn't  work against the miami dolphins it did  work after that in the wins over the  rams and the new england patriots and  back to nick mullins look he was  adequate against the jets when he came  in when garoppolo was injured the first  time he beat the giants the next week  and then there was that game against the  eagles where you know he throws the ball  to the other team as if he's playing for  the eagles that night and that caused  him to fall to number three on the depth  chart and at some point in the past  couple of weeks the 49ers decided to go  week by week deciding which of the two  backups would be the number two guy  depending upon the match up and it  wasn't a competition between the two  some weeks kyle shanahan thought it  would be better for beathard other weeks  better for mullins remains to be seen  who gets the start on thursday night  against the green bay packers though  mullins is the one who came in on sunday  but garoppolo now you have to wonder  number one will they have him beyond  this season number two we'll even play  again this season because if this goes  downhill for them and remember there's  still only three games into the seven  game death march if this goes downhill  for them  maybe they just decide not to put him  back on the field maybe they decide to  just let that ankle heal completely and  entirely so  when the time comes to try to trade him  in the offseason shireen he's not still  recovering from any type of injury he's  100  when march rolls around he's got two  years left on his contract salaries of  24.1 million next year 24.2 million the  year after that i won't be surprised if  they try to trade him they may not be  able to find any takers maybe they have  to pay some of the salary to get him off  the books but regardless the way it's  going now i don't think he'll be back  next year they'll look at their options  and there's the schedule  for the next four weeks while garoppolo  is out packers at saints at rams bills  it doesn't soften up until after that  with washington and the cowboys and then  they finish strong  from an opponent's standpoint against  the cardinals in the seahawks so it  feels like the beginning of the end  frankly for jimmy garoppolo in san  francisco  the good thing for them mike and why  they may bring him back is ultimately  they're going to get most of these  players back i realize nick bose is not  coming back who you really need as a  pass rusher but they're going to get a  lot of these guys back you figure  kittles will be healthy enough by the  end of the year to come back debo samuel  is going to miss another game but he'll  be back if you get all those guys back  this is not a team i would want to play  in the playoffs so if they can get  healthy and actually make the plows even  if they get that last extra playoff spot  as a wild card team  it's not a team i want to face because  they have all this playoff experience  they were really good last year and and  you hope that they are they hope at that  point that they're really healthy and  can win a playoff game so that's the  only thing i think the extra wild card  team and the fact that they could get  healthy by the end of the year  could bring all these guys back and  maybe they think by playoff time we're  really rolling and we're starting to  play well again but other than that i  mean the next few games are going to  determine to me they have to beat the  rams that's that that is a must-win game  for them on that schedule when you start  looking at possible w's and l's i think  they have to win that game they start  losing a bunch of these games then yeah  it's not worth bringing any of these  guys back for this season i mean let's  be realistic about where they've  struggled this year they've  they beat the rams the first time but  they lost to the seahawks they lost to  the cardinals they play both of them  again i just think it's going to be very  difficult for them to position  themselves  for  a playoff spot when you consider they're  in last place at four and four  and and i i think that seahawks  cardinals rams will have a good chance  to get there  but either the saints or the buccaneers  will be getting one of those wild card  spots i don't see the 49ers catching new  orleans or san francisco they've got a  game coming up against new orleans that  will be critical see what the 49ers need  to hope for is that  they their separation  in the nfc south and the second place  team starts to fade so they can maybe be  picked off by the 49ers that's  unless they're going to leapfrog the  rams  or the cardinals their best shot is to  hope that the second place team in the  nfc south fades away because look the  bears are starting to free fall there  isn't going to be a second place team  from the nfc east that is in contention  it's too late for the vikings at two and  five i think to get into the playoff  hunt the 49ers number one they're going  to need to win and number two they need  to start  thinking about not that they will i mean  somebody in the organization perak  marathi or someone will have it all  figured out all the different  permutations and ways to get in all they  can take care of is winning games but  that they  you know yeah if they were on the table  they won't have a problem at 12 and four  but we've seen them without these help  without their key players we've seen  what it looks like my only hesitation is  every time it feels like they're down  kyle shanahan finds a way to spring them  back to life and every time you give up  on the 49ers they rip off a couple of  wins and look great and then you start  buying into it and then it goes the  other way  yeah that's exactly right mike and  that's what's happened this whole year  to them and and it has been just one  entry after another we talked about the  running back depth  last week because they had all the  running backs who were injured and now  it's the quarterback again and then it's  the tight end and eventually you run out  of guys i mean they to me have been the  most injury plug team and i know the  cowboys and the broncos have had injury  issues but really when you look at the  49ers there's just been one guy after  another and and some of them are season  ending and i just don't eventually you  just can't overcome all those injuries  and  let's face it a lot in this league has  to do with availability and who has the  healthiest team and this year with kovid  thrown in there who doesn't get coveted  who doesn't have the issues and right  now it's the steelers who who've been  the healthiest and done all the right  things and and so far that's why they're  they're the lone undefeated team there  have been others but they have been  truly healthy this year for the most  part and i think that's really played a  big part in where they are  and the 49ers could draw a lucky card on  thursday night as it relates to covet  because the packers have an issue that  is still emerging and who knows whether  they'll even be able to play this game  on thursday night we'll talk about that  coming up one last thing about the 49ers  and keep this in mind in march they  evaluated the possibility of signing tom  brady they were very transparent about  it they told jimmy garoppolo they talked  publicly about it but what that was was  a shot across the ballot jimmy garoppolo  it was a you better step up or you're  going to be stepping off and i think  they are going to evaluate all options  all opportunities some have suggested a  matt ryan jimmy garoppolo reunion in san  francisco others like me have said maybe  that's where kirk cousins will end up  that's the guy that garoppolo or that  shanahan thought he was going to get  three years ago when they traded for  garoppolo right around the trade  deadline so  i think all options are on the table for  the 49ers at the quarterback position  next year as they try to reload on the  fly  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

